# Austin Allegro four-door saloon, 1973-1982.
#
# The Allegro: the Marina-replacing front-wheel-drive saloon with the
# Hydragas suspension and the much-criticised styling, on sale in Britain from
# 17 May 1973. The Series 2 four-door saloon is modelled, the shell the
# photographs show; the two-door, the estate, the Vanden Plas and the Equipe
# are not separately represented. The quartic steering wheel was dropped before
# this car and is not modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austin_Allegro
#
# Dimensions 3.861 x 1.600 x 1.397 m, wheelbase 2.438 m (period UK figures).
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a true level side elevation with the camera at
# about hub height and the front bumper tip clipped at the frame edge. That
# car is New Zealand CKD assembly; the three-quarter and rear photographs are
# a UK Series 2 car and govern the grille, lamps and trim.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no UK colour list was read. White, Red, Blue and Brown
# are plain period names. Weights 14, 12, 10, 8, total 44, provisional.
#
# Speed 145 km/h. Comfort 50/405, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 50. Classes 0,1.
# Dates: intro May 1973; retires staggered 1992-1995 as a road tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/austin-allegro.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/austin-allegro.dae. References:
# citycars/references/austin-allegro/ (gitignored).
#
# Accepted deviations: the level New Zealand CKD profile has a clipped front
# bumper tip and is used for the shell only; the UK photographs govern the
# Series 2 trim. The Series 2 appearance represents the whole 1973-82 range.
# The grille recess is a dark bed with raised trim, and the rear bright strips
# bow slightly more than in the photograph.


